  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan ratified the instruments of the Freedom of Association and Protection of the Right to Organise Convention, 1948 (No. 87); P029 - Protocol of 2014 to the Forced Labour Convention, 1930; and the Tripartite Consultation (International Labour Standards) Convention, 1976 (No. 144). Ratifications were  registered at the ILO on 17 March 2021. For the ratification of Conventions and the Protocol, the ILO provided technical inputs such as awareness and capacity building activities of the tripartite constituents and other relevant stakeholders through tripartite consultation, training and advocacy.

The ILO provided direct technical advisory services to the Minister and the Ministry, including the correct format of the instruments of ratification for their registration at the ILO.  The ILO provided assistance from January 2019 to March 2021. The ratifications were announced, at a ceremony with the ILO DG on 11 June 2021.

With respect to the new Trade Union Act, the ILO provided HQ and DWT technical assistance (preliminary comments; technical memoranda on several aspects of principles of freedom of association; translation of different drafts of the new Bill) as well as a technical review of national laws and the drafting and review of a new Trade Union Act. The aim of the new Act is to bring it  into conformity with the provisions of Convention No. 87.</narrative>
   </description>
